Survive a TCP client disconnecting mid-reply.

Upstream exits the whole simulator (exit -10) when a write to the client
fails, which happens whenever a client disconnects while a reply is on its
way (e.g. a host watchdog closing the link). Drop that client and wait for
the next one instead.

diff --git a/src/simulator.c b/src/simulator.c
index a73f110..212b7ed 100644
--- a/src/simulator.c
+++ b/src/simulator.c
@@ -261,8 +261,12 @@ void sim_socket_out (uint8_t data)
         }
 #else
         if(sim.socket_fd) {
-            if(write(sim.socket_fd, buf, len) < 0)
-                exit(-10);
+            if(write(sim.socket_fd, buf, len) < 0) {
+                // Client went away mid-reply: drop it and wait for the next
+                // one instead of exiting (sim_socket_in accepts when fd is 0).
+                close(sim.socket_fd);
+                sim.socket_fd = 0;
+            }
         }
 #endif
         // don't print comment on next line if we are just printing to avoid buffer overflow
